From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm] Skip libtorch_cpu RTLD_GLOBAL promotion when rocm_sdk
 is installed

Version-locked to VLLM_REF=v0.30.0 (`git apply --check` clean).
Upstream #56190 ("[ROCm][Bugfix] Fix profiler in TheRock image", new in
v0.30.0) preloads libtorch_cpu.so RTLD_GLOBAL at `import vllm` time so
kineto can advertise itself to rocprofiler-sdk. On this stack (TheRock
torch 2.13 + `rocm` pip package) that preload is fatal: libtorch_cpu
statically links LLVM, and _rocm_sdk_core (loaded later via
torch._rocm_init -> rocm_sdk) registers the same cl::opt options a
second time -> "Option 'spirv-expand-step' registered more than once" ->
LLVM ERROR -> abort during `import vllm` (exit 139; the server
crash-loops before logging anything). Skipping the preload when
rocm_sdk is present restores v0.29.0 behavior; it costs only the kineto
GPU-profiling registration, which this stack does not use. Where
rocm_sdk is absent the upstream fix stays active. Drop this patch when
a pinned VLLM_REF guards or reverts #56190.
---
diff --git a/vllm/env_override.py b/vllm/env_override.py
--- a/vllm/env_override.py
+++ b/vllm/env_override.py
@@ -114,6 +114,18 @@ def _maybe_promote_torch_symbols_for_rocm():
     if _get_torch_version_attr("hip") is None:
         return
+    # Local: skip the RTLD_GLOBAL preload when rocm_sdk is installed
+    # (TheRock torch + `rocm` pip package). libtorch_cpu.so statically
+    # links LLVM; preloading it globally registers cl::opt options that
+    # _rocm_sdk_core (loaded later via torch._rocm_init -> rocm_sdk)
+    # registers a second time -> "Option 'spirv-expand-step' registered
+    # more than once" -> LLVM ERROR -> abort during `import vllm`
+    # (exit 139, server crash-loops before logging anything). Restores
+    # v0.29.0 behavior; costs only kineto GPU-profiling registration,
+    # which this stack does not use. Upstream #56190 has no fix yet;
+    # drop this hunk if a pinned VLLM_REF guards or reverts it.
+    if importlib.util.find_spec("rocm_sdk") is not None:
+        return
     try:
         import ctypes
         import glob

